# Vendored third-party files must round-trip byte for byte.
#
# upstream/README.md tells a later session to verify these five files by SHA256
# against obra/superpowers. With core.autocrlf=true and no attribute, a checkout
# on Windows rewrites LF to CRLF, every file grows, and every hash check fails
# for a reason that has nothing to do with CDD — which is exactly the kind of
# silent divergence the vendoring note exists to prevent.
upstream/** -text

# The installed skill bundle is validated by sync.ps1's hash comparison and its
# SKILL.md is parsed from disk as YAML frontmatter. Pin LF so a Windows checkout
# produces exactly the bytes that were tested, rather than a CRLF variant whose
# frontmatter has never been through the loader.
skill/** -text
